<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pactum Lotharii</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/840">840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pactum Lotharii was an agreement of 23 February 840 between the Frankish emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair I</a> and the Venetian doge Pietro Tradonico. It regulated borders, trade, justice and the return of fugitives between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the Carolingian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and is the oldest surviving Venetian diplomatic document. It treated Venice as a separate partner rather than a Byzantine dependency.</p></div>
